[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/land/auto-deploy.ts",
  "line": 87,
  "title": "A rollback after the new release boots is never recorded",
  "detail": "At boot the daemon clears the persisted attempt as soon as bootSha equals attempt.sha, but the deploy job is still health-checking that new daemon. If the health check then fails and `limitless deploy` rolls back (src/cli/service.ts), the rolled-back daemon finds no attempt: nothing is blocked and the feed never says the deploy failed. The reverse also happens: a boot on the old SHA while the job is still running declares failure early. The job's exit status (its status file) is the only authority for the outcome, and the caller that reads it is killed by the restart. Keep the attempt (with its job id) until its terminal status has been read; at boot and on later ticks, reconcile an unfinished attempt from that job's status file, recording success, or a block plus a deploy.failed feed item with the redacted log tail. Add tests: target boots then the job reports failure (rollback): blocked and reported; old-SHA boot while the job is still running: not judged until the status exists."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/land/deploy-process.ts",
  "line": 93,
  "title": "A deploy job that never writes its status stalls automatic deploys forever",
  "detail": "deployProcess polls the status file with no deadline and no check that the launchd job still exists, so a job that was removed, crashed before writing its status, or hung leaves AutoDeploy's `running` flag set and no later landing ever deploys; and removeDeployJob skips jobs without a status while the boot reconcile forgets the job id. Bound the wait (a deadline above `limitless deploy`'s own maximum) and detect a job that no longer exists (for example `launchctl list <label>` failing); either way record a block with a clear reason and remove the job, and keep the job id durable until its removal has succeeded. Add tests for a missing job and a deadline."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/land/deploy-process.ts",
